                  <provenance type="#l" source="5698"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_588">Wilton, Wiltshire.
                        Abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St Edith, of Benedictine nuns</orgName><p>Includes prayers for the abbess of Wilton in the litany, and
                        for the congregation of St Mary and St Edith (fol. 206r). Cf. Burlington Ho.
                        Exhib. 1908 no. 42 and E. G. Millar, Les MSS. à peintures des bibliothèques
                        de Londres (Paris 1914--1920), pp. 48--61 and A. G. Little.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given in 1523 by Ranfe Lepton, parson of
                     Alresford and Kingsworthy, to Elizabeth Langrege, of Romsey. An Elizabeth
                     Langriche aged 17 was professed a nun of Romsey 28 July 1534 (Reg. Stephen
                     Gardiner, p. 39). See also under Romsey.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">"Nicholaus Saunder" (front flyleaf,
                     1581).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Marquis of Dorchester gave to the College
                     1680--1687.</provenance>
               <provenance type="#i" source="6741"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_470">Romsey, Hampshire.
                        Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin and St Elfleda, of Benedictine nuns</orgName><p>"The Xth day of October yn the yere of our lord' God' oon'
                        Thousand five hundreth' and XXIII the XVth yere of kyng Henry the viiith and
                        the XXIIIth yere of the Translacion' of my lord' Rychard Foxe Bysshop of
                        Wynchestre Maister Ranfe lepton' parson of Alresford' and of Kyng'worthy
                        servaunt and Chapelayne to my sayde lord' Richard' gave thys boke to
                        Elizabeth langrege whos Granfader John Warner gentylman' was Uncle to my
                        lady Dame Anne Westbroke Abbes of Romsey to the saide Elizabeth' Mynchynne
                        of Romsey the saide Maister Ranfe was grete uncle unto...' (fol.
                     144).</p></provenance>
